<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity up 0.18pct week to Jan 24.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity up 0.18pct week to Jan 24.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's central bank said liquidity in the banking system grew 0.18 percent, or 32 million sucres, to 17.08 billion sucres in the week to January 24.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the bank sector ended 1996 at 16.99 billion sucres, up 35.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
